      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "JAY TEE TYRON NZ (7) was successful last start by 4.5 metres in a nice return to form at Redcliffe over 1780m. Must overcome a very wide draw and this looks a sterner test than last time but he has spaced them there and is capable of another big performance. THE CASUAL GOOSE (10) made a winning return at his latest appearance a week-and-a-half ago, getting home by 5 metres over 1850m at Marburg. May just need a bit of luck at some point from this difficult draw but he is fitter for that last hit-out and capable of making it consecutive wins. COPY WRITER (3) is worth another chance after a last-start eighth over 1780m at Redcliffe a month ago while THREE CHORD RIFF (2) is the best of the rest after finishing fourth, also over 1780m at Redcliffe, last time out.",
